NON-LINEAR across the document: equal value vectors are ONE hole with several sites; a key present in some instances is a PRESENCE hole and its body is generalized over those; `R.instantiate(i)` rebuilds instance i (`A.kv_eq_keyed(R.instantiate(i), x, 'name')`). Consumers: `drift.anchor` (keyed), `helmfile.family`. Measured on microservices-demo@b9a978db kubernetes-manifests: Deployment ×12 → 31 holes (13 value / 18 presence), 51 sites, rebuild 12/12; ×10 (minus redis-cart, loadgenerator) → 24 (11/13), 43 sites; Service ×12 → 8; ServiceAccount ×11 → 1. The largest presence hole is the FRONTEND variant (7 sites: its env vars and both httpGet probes) — a flag the Helm chart does not have. CART-0872 |\n| Where does a Helm chart HARDCODE what varies across the plain manifests it should produce — the lines to extend the chart at — and which of its knobs does the corpus never turn? | `:CartographHelmBase {manifests} [chart]` (quickfix: one item per template line holding a literal where the manifests vary). In Lua `local B = require 'cartograph.helmbase'; local r = B.diff(<chart>, <manifests dir>); print(table.concat(B.lines(r), '\\n'))` — the AUTHORED base is the chart rendered with no values (helmprov symbolic), the INFERRED base the manifests' keyed generalization (`kv_generalize`, per kind); documents pair by FILE NAME (`templates/<x>.yaml` with `<manifests>/<x>.yaml`) and by ORDINAL within a kind (an authored name is a placeholder). Every spot that VARIES across the manifests is, in the chart, `param` (a placeholder there, also inside a string), `block` (a placeholder above it: `toYaml .Values.x.resources`), `hardcoded` (a literal — located through helmprov's spans: `r.sites[i].at` = { \"templates/x.yaml:74\" }), `absent`, or `mixed` (which documents differ is named); `r.knobs` = chart placeholders where every manifest agrees and nothing varies below. ⚠ \"varies\" is relative to the corpus (one deployment per service makes a service name a constant); keyed alignment is only as good as the merge key (loadgenerator's `main` container is not `server`). Measured on microservices-demo (helm-chart vs kubernetes-manifests): 35 paired documents, 25 varying spots — 8 parameter, 4 block, 11 HARDCODED (container port, PORT env, gRPC probe ports, probe timings, Service type and ports: 81 template lines), 2 mixed (the chart's redis-cart Deployment and frontend-external Service lack the `app` label the manifests carry), 19 knobs never turned (peer service names in the ADDR env values). CART-0873 |\n","before":"| Across a SET of data documents (every Deployment in a directory, every release's values), what is shared and what VARIES — which spots are ONE parameter (the same value vector at several sites), which keys only some documents have? | `local A = require('cartograph.algebra').load(); local R = A.kv_generalize(<values: yamlvalue documents>, { keyfield = 'name' })` → `R.template` (objects aligned BY KEY, arrays of objects by their merge key — k8s `name` — other arrays positionally, else one hole), `R.holes` = { { id, kind = 'value' \\| 'presence', values = per-instance vector, sites = { '$.spec…' } } } — NON-LINEAR across the document: equal value vectors are ONE hole with several sites; a key present in some instances is a PRESENCE hole and its body is generalized over those; `R.instantiate(i)` rebuilds instance i (`A.kv_eq_keyed(R.instantiate(i), x, 'name')`). Consumers: `drift.anchor` (keyed), `helmfile.family`. Measured on microservices-demo@b9a978db kubernetes-manifests: Deployment ×12 → 31 holes (13 value / 18 presence), 51 sites, rebuild 12/12; ×10 (minus redis-cart, loadgenerator) → 24 (11/13), 43 sites; Service ×12 → 8; ServiceAccount ×11 → 1. The largest presence hole is the FRONTEND variant (7 sites: its env vars and both httpGet probes) — a flag the Helm chart does not have. CART-0872 |\n","file":".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"},"touched":[".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"],"verb":"edit"},